This package contains weights derived from, and files that depend on, two models released by Alibaba Cloud's Qwen team
under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Thinking-2507   https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Thinking-2507
  Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507   https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507

The Qwen repositories carry the Apache License 2.0 with the notice "Copyright 2024 Alibaba Cloud". A copy of the
license text is in LICENSE.

Changes made to the Qwen weights (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)):

  model/Qwen3-4B-Thinking-Concise-bf16.gguf
      The weights of Qwen3-4B-Thinking-2507 with a low-rank part of the difference between that model and
      Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 subtracted (the "q80 piece", described in README.md), written as a bf16 GGUF file. The
      tokenizer, chat template and architecture are unchanged.
  piece/P_q80.safetensors
      The part that was subtracted, derived from the weight difference between the two Qwen models, stored as bf16
      low-rank factors and whole tensors.
  router/*.pt
      Small classifiers trained on answers produced by models derived from the two Qwen models. Question vectors in
      router/embed*.pt are the layer-18 hidden states of Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 (the output of its first 18 decoder
      layers), averaged over the question's tokens.

Everything else in this package (the scripts, the documentation and the result files) is original work, Copyright 2026
Loxley Labs, produced with Claude Code, and is released under the same Apache License 2.0.

Loxley Labs is not affiliated with Alibaba Cloud or the Qwen team, and they have not reviewed or endorsed this package.
"Qwen" is used only to name the models this work started from.

code/ifeval_patch.diff is a patch to two files of the IFEval checker from Google's google-research repository (Apache
License 2.0) and contains short excerpts of them.

The refusal check in safety/ and the evaluation scripts in code/ read public datasets that are not included here
(AdvBench, XSTest, GSM8K, MATH-500, BIG-Bench Hard, MMLU, IFEval); each keeps its own licence, listed in README.md.
